   "title": "Headache red flags (SNNOOP10)",
   "target": "History_present_illness",
   "alert": "Red flag for a secondary headache: look for a cause today. Sudden (thunderclap) onset, fever with neck stiffness, a new neurological deficit, reduced consciousness or papilloedema need same-day emergency assessment with brain imaging, and lumbar puncture if indicated. New headache after 50: check ESR and CRP for giant cell arteritis.",
